<section background-color="heading">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item colspan="39" vertical-align="center">
      <p role="eyebrow">The decision</p>
      <h1 font-size="40pt">Make room for a restorative hour</h1>
      <p font-size="lg"><b>The proposal is not to build a spa. It is to test one memorable, well-run hour that belongs to this property.</b></p>
      <grid direction="vertical" divider="sm palette-1" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item padding="8pt 0">
          <h4>Name an owner</h4>
          <p font-size="sm">Appoint one property sponsor for guest experience, operations, and the pilot decision.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item padding="8pt 0">
          <h4>Name the room and rhythm</h4>
          <p font-size="sm">Identify a suitable flexible space and the session times that fit the stay.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item padding="8pt 0">
          <h4>Agree the evidence</h4>
          <p font-size="sm">Replace the illustrative assumptions with property costs, pricing, capacity, and success gates.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <spacer mode="fixed" size="14pt"/>
      <p font-size="sm">The next working session should leave the team with a chosen ritual, accountable roles, a costed scenario, and a clear go-or-no-go pilot decision.</p>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="21" padding="0">
      <ai-image prompt="Quiet editorial hospitality photograph of a boutique hotel terrace prepared for one restorative hour, a staff member's hand opening the door toward two simple chairs, a journal, tea glass and folded white throw, soft late-afternoon natural light, crisp white and sea-glass palette with deep teal shadows, no people posing, no text or logos" image-style="restorative-hospitality-editorial" aspect-ratio="portrait" background="true"/>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>